# E8 image build context (ADR-004 section 5a, E8): an ALLOW-LIST. Everything is excluded, then exactly what the program, its libraries and the scripts need is let back in.
# BuildKit reads this file next to the Dockerfile when the build is started from the repository root with -f:
#   docker build -f docs/refactoring/suffix-tree-upgrade/analysis/e8/Dockerfile .
# Nothing of .git (history, remotes, configuration), wiki, tests, other docs or any bin / obj directory enters the image or the build cache.
*
# the program: apps/SuffixTree.EmProto, the two product libraries it references, the linked sources of the benchmark project
!apps/SuffixTree.EmProto
!apps/SuffixTree.Esa.Bench/PairedStats.cs
!apps/SuffixTree.Esa.Bench/Links
!src/SuffixTree/Algorithms/SuffixTree.Esa
!src/SuffixTree/Algorithms/SuffixTree.Core
# the style rules the projects read (.editorconfig); the root Directory.Build.props and Directory.Packages.props are NOT sent: the Dockerfile supplies its own props (no package restore from the network)
!.editorconfig
# the scripts and the props of the image
!docs/refactoring/suffix-tree-upgrade/analysis/e8
# whatever sits inside the allowed directories and must not enter: build output, the author's data and mutation work
**/bin
**/obj
**/mutation
**/*.tsv
**/*.sums
**/__pycache__
